    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAs">III As</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q">Quintum: qui ex hoc discedat, sit dignus eorum que in scripto pacis dicuntur (habentur), quod apud Greateleiam institutum est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="5" corresp="#wit-q">Quintum, qui ex hoc descedat, sit dignus eorum quæ in scripto pacis dicuntur, quod apud Greateleiam institutum est.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">Fifthly, he who neglects this shall be liable to those [punishments] which are stated in the statute relating to to the public peace, which was drawn up at Grately.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares II As 25.2.</note>
      </div>
